---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Prose from '../../components/Prose.astro';
import { currentSite } from '../../data/sites.mjs';
import { PUBLISHER, CONTACT_CONSENT, SMS_CONSENT_LABEL } from '../../data/brand.mjs';

/*
 * NOT REVIEWED BY AN ATTORNEY. Written conservatively for that reason: it
 * describes only what the site actually does, and where a broad permission
 * and a narrow one were both possible it takes the narrow one.
 *
 * CALL_RECORDING must match the phone system. Calls are not recorded today.
 * If that ever changes, this page changes first, together with the spoken
 * notice on the line itself.
 */
const CALL_RECORDING = false;

const site = currentSite();
const us = PUBLISHER.legalName ?? site.siteName;
const updated = 'October 2026';
---

<Base title="Privacy Policy" description={`How ${site.siteName} handles the information you send.`} path="/privacy">
  <div class="page section">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated {updated}</p>
    <Prose>
      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        When you send a trip request we collect what you type: your name, phone number, email address
        if you give one, your date, your group size, the occasion, and any notes. If you call the
        number on this site, our phone system records the number you called from and the time and
        length of the call.
        {CALL_RECORDING ? ' Calls may be recorded, and you will hear a notice at the start of the call.' : ' Calls are not recorded.'}
      </p>
      <p>
        Our hosting provider records basic technical information, such as the type of browser used to
        load a page. We do not use it to identify you. We do not ask for payment details, and you
        should never send them to us.
      </p>

      <h2>What we do with it</h2>
      <p>
        We use your request to arrange your trip. That means a person on our side reads it, may call
        or email you about it, and passes it to one local boat operator on {site.marketName} so they
        can contact you about the trip. We do not sell your information, and we do not pass a request
        to more than one operator.
      </p>
      <p>This is the consent shown above the button on the form:</p>
      <blockquote>{CONTACT_CONSENT}</blockquote>
      <p>
        Texting is separate. We only text you if you tick the box that says: "{SMS_CONSENT_LABEL}"
        Reply STOP to any text and we stop.
      </p>

      <h2>Who else handles it</h2>
      <p>
        Requests are stored in our customer management system, which a software company runs for us,
        and the site is hosted by a web hosting company. Both handle your information only to provide
        that service to us. The operator who receives your request handles it under their own
        privacy terms once they have it.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        We keep requests while they are useful for arranging trips and for our records with the
        operator, and delete them when they are not. You can ask us to delete yours at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask what we hold about you, ask us to correct it, ask us to delete it, or tell us to
        stop contacting you. Use the request form and say so in the notes, or call the number on this
        site. We will also tell the operator who received your request to stop.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>This site is published by {us}.</p>
    </Prose>
  </div>
</Base>
